// Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
//   boardName "RP2040" -> designer/boards/RP2040/RP2040.json -> const RP2040Data = {...}
//
// pfodWeb NOTE (button/LED/NeoPixel tagging audit, 2026-07-13):
//
// Board: "Sea-Picro" by Josh Johnson (github.com/joshajohnson/sea-picro) —
// an RP2040 board in the Arduino Pro Micro form factor, designed as a
// drop-in replacement for ATmega32u4-based Pro Micros in keyboards (also
// sold assembled by beekeeb, shop.beekeeb.com/products/sea-picro). This
// repo's variants/rp2040/boards.txt lists it as "Generic Sea-Picro"
// (build.variant=sea_picro, build.led= — empty, confirming no plain LED
// pin is registered for this board at the Arduino core level either).
//
// This board's own pins_arduino.h (comment header, verbatim):
//   "Pin definitions taken from:
//    https://github.com/joshajohnson/sea-picro/blob/master/documentation/
//    pinout/sea-picro-top-pinout-rory-render.png"
// and declares:
//   #define PIN_LED (31u)         // comment directly above: "LEDs not pinned out"
//   #define PIN_NEOPIXEL (25u)
//
// GPIO31 / PIN_LED - CONFIRMED NOT A REAL PIN, no chipGpios entry added
// (deliberately):
// RP2040 silicon only implements GPIO0-29 — GPIO31 does not exist on the
// real chip. This board's own pins_arduino.h source comment states
// verbatim "LEDs not pinned out" directly above the PIN_LED (31u)
// #define, i.e. the vendor's own header already documents this as a
// placeholder/sentinel, not a real onboard LED. The same 31 sentinel is
// reused for PIN_SERIAL2_TX/PIN_SERIAL2_RX ("Not pinned out") and
// PIN_WIRE1_SDA/SCL — consistent with the "31 = not pinned out" idiom used
// throughout the arduino-pico RP2040 board family (e.g.
// sparkfun_promicrorp2040/pins_arduino.h uses the identical 31 sentinel
// for its unrouted PIN_SPI1_*/PIN_WIRE1_* pins). This board's own
// generic_full/common.h D-alias fallback only covers D0-D29 (no D30/D31),
// and no other static const uint8_t alias anywhere in this board's headers
// resolves to 31, so build_boards.js's parser never adds a "GPIO31" pin to
// the Designer's pin list for this board in the first place — matching
// the identical situation already confirmed for the sibling board
// sparkfun_micromodrp2040 (its PIN_NEOPIXEL=31 sentinel, see that board's
// board.json for the full parser-behaviour rationale). Adding a chipGpios
// entry here would be the one thing that could wrongly introduce a
// nonexistent GPIO31 pin, so none is added.
// Cross-checked against the vendor's own pinout render referenced in the
// pins_arduino.h header comment (joshajohnson/sea-picro repo) and the
// project's public README/product pages (github.com/joshajohnson/sea-picro,
// joshajohnson.com/sea-picro, shop.beekeeb.com/products/sea-picro): the
// "RST" variant is described as having "a WS2812 LED for use with
// CircuitPython or as a status indicator" plus a separate passive "onboard
// power LED" (not GPIO-controlled — a hardware power-presence indicator,
// same out-of-scope category as the power LEDs on other boards already
// audited in this family, e.g. sparkfun_promicrorp2040). No separate
// GPIO-driven plain/simple LED distinct from the WS2812 is documented
// anywhere — consistent with pins_arduino.h's own "LEDs not pinned out"
// comment.
//
// GPIO25 / PIN_NEOPIXEL - CONFIRMED, tagged below:
// The Sea-Picro's onboard addressable WS2812 LED is documented in the
// project's own README/product pages as being driven via GPIO25 (the
// "EXT" variant's dedicated 5V-level-shifted RGB output pin for driving
// external WS2812 strings is explicitly identified as GPIO25 in the
// project documentation; the "RST" variant's onboard WS2812 status LED
// uses the same PIN_NEOPIXEL=25 definition in this shared pins_arduino.h).
// This matches the PIN_NEOPIXEL (25u) value declared directly in this
// board's own pins_arduino.h. Tagged "led_neopixel" (not led_high/led_low,
// since it is one addressable WS2812 pixel, not a simple on/off LED) —
// matches this repo's existing led_neopixel precedent, e.g.
// sparkfun_promicrorp2040/board.json GPIO25 and
// rp2040w/sparkfun_thingplusrp2350/board.json GPIO14. pwm_output is kept
// (not omitted) because arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040
// GPIO regardless of NeoPixel usage, matching that precedent exactly.
// digital_input is dropped, matching the same precedent's rationale (a
// WS2812 data pin is not meaningfully readable as a plain digital input).
// No collision with any SPI/Wire bus alias on this board — this board's
// pins_arduino.h SPI0 (MISO 20/MOSI 23/SCK 22/SS 21), SPI1 (MISO 12/MOSI
// 13/SCK 14/SS 15), and Wire0 (SDA 4/SCL 5) / Wire1 (SDA 2/SCL 3, "not
// pinned out") aliases are all distinct from GPIO25, so no bus-capability
// contamination bug applies here.
//
// No onboard general-purpose button beyond the dedicated single-button
// reset/bootloader circuit described in the project's own
// README/documentation ("a single button reset / bootloader circuit which
// changes behavior based on how long it's held... tap for <500ms to
// reset, hold >1s to enter bootloader mode"). This is explicitly a
// dedicated hardware reset/BOOTSEL circuit, not a normal user-readable
// GPIO — out of scope for GPIO capability tagging, same precedent as every
// other RP2040 board's BOOTSEL/reset button in this repo (e.g.
// rpipico/board.json, sparkfun_promicrorp2040/board.json).
//
// Full findings/sources trail:
// boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040/sea_picro/notes.txt
{
  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name) — for this board that's
  // "Generic Sea-Picro" (variants/rp2040/boards.txt).
  "boardName": "RP2040",
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)",

  // Same parser dialect as every other RP2040 board — see
  // ../board.json for the full rationale.
  "family": "rp2040",

  // No genuinely bidirectional-but-input-only pins on this board.
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports — Serial only. This is the plain (non-WiFi)
  // "rp2040" chip bucket; the Sea-Picro has no onboard WiFi radio.
  "connections": ["serial"],

  "pinNotes": {},

  "chipGpios": {
    "25": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "led_neopixel", "pwm_output"], "note": "PIN_NEOPIXEL — onboard WS2812 addressable RGB LED / status indicator. Confirmed via the Sea-Picro project's own README/product documentation (see pfodWeb NOTE above). PIN_LED (31u) is a vendor-documented \"LEDs not pinned out\" placeholder — GPIO31 does not exist on real RP2040 silicon (GPIO0-29 only) and is left untagged." }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2040/RP2350.
  "dac": {},

  // RP2040's one 12-bit ADC (0-4095), ~3.3V reference — same as every
  // other RP2040 board.
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
